 was done using an inductively coupled plasma-optical emission spectrometer (ICP-OES) (Agilent, USA). The total metal content of Zn–Mn and Ni–Cd batteries is shown in Table 1.\"], \"case_id\": \"znmn-nicd-bioleaching\", \"paper\": \"Bioleaching of Spent Zn–mn or Ni–cd Batteries by Aspergillus Species\", \"node_id\": \"http://weee-kg.org/source:Bioleaching%20of%20Spent%20Zn%E2%80%93mn%20or%20Ni%E2%80%93cd%20Batteries%20by%20Aspergillus%20Species:Component_Zn_Mn_battery\"}" ;
    analysis:state "Dismantled electrode powder; mixed, dried, milled and sieved below 200 µm" ;
